{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1791272564,"nonce":"YsLhqT+w4x9ob0k3Biki8z0U8LU=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"UCE_lAHOULtcMc8AAAABVIs2AM7-YKDV","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"6d2631134a85dc9e11c1c3d644438358eaaed194e1c7808cd41c55f6470e291a"},"target":"03325e07eaa63f6d0a6cbd156aac9b690486beb13769d310f38414c2b8403aa3","message":"**TL;DR**\n- **What:** automated checks that really gate every change.\n- **Why:** tests never run, nothing blocks a bad merge, and there's no security scanning.\n- **User impact:** fewer bugs on the live site.\n- **Effort:** medium.\n\n---\n\n**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nCI is green, but it checks much less than it appears to:\n\n- **Tests never run.** `npm test` (50 `node:test` tests) is not called by `.github/workflows/checks.yml` or by the pre-commit hook.\n- **The format check can't fail.** `frontend-format` in `lefthook.yml` runs `prettier --write … \u0026\u0026 git add`, which rewrites files and exits 0. Proof: `frontend/src/env.d.ts` has been unformatted since the initial commit, and the job is green on every run.\n- **The commands are defined in the wrong place.** They live only in `lefthook.yml`, and `npm run typecheck` / `npm run lint` call into lefthook. CI depends on the git-hook tool instead of the other way round, and the frontend README has to tell people to bypass `npm run format` because it stages files.\n- **Lint coverage is partial and the config is a template.** Lefthook only covers `frontend/src`, so `frontend/tests/` is never linted or format-checked. The ESLint config is the Quasar template: `flat/essential`, `recommendedTypeChecked`, and Cordova/Capacitor/BEX/Google Analytics globals.\n- **Installs aren't reproducible.** The checks run `make install` (`npm install`, no cache), while Pages and Docker run `npm ci`. Node is `24` in the checks and `lts/*` in Pages.\n- **Nothing stops a bad merge or deploy.** `dev` and `main` have no branch protection, so PRs merge with failing checks, and Pages deploys every push to `main`. A type or lint error does fail `quasar build` through `vite-plugin-checker`; a failing test or bad formatting does not.\n- **No dependency or security scanning:** no Dependabot, no `npm audit`, no CodeQL, no secret scanning.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\nRefactor first (no behaviour change), then add the new gates.\n\n1. **npm scripts are the single definition.** In `frontend/package.json`:\n   - `test`: unchanged\n   - `typecheck`: `vue-tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.typecheck.json`\n   - `lint`: `eslint .`\n   - `format`: `prettier --write .` and `format:check`: `prettier --check .`\n\n   Lefthook and CI both call these scripts (pre-commit may keep fixing staged files). Add `frontend/.nvmrc` (24) and use it in every workflow and the Dockerfile.\n2. **ESLint and Prettier.** Replace the template config with:\n   ```js\n   js.configs.recommended,\n   pluginVue.configs['flat/recommended'],\n   vueTsConfigs.recommended,\n   prettier, // eslint-config-prettier, replaces @vue/eslint-config-prettier/skip-formatting\n   ```\n   - Add `ignores` for `dist/`, `.quasar/` and `quasar.config.*.temporary.compiled*`.\n   - Give Node globals only to `quasar.config.ts` and scripts, and drop the Cordova/Capacitor/BEX/`ga` globals.\n   - Decide whether `tests/` is linted; it should at least be format-checked.\n   - Fix whatever `flat/recommended` flags in the same PR.\n   - Reference: `EPFL-ENAC/co2-calculator` `frontend/eslint.config.js`.\n3. **A quality workflow that gates PRs** (replaces `checks.yml`). On `pull_request` to `dev` and `main`: `npm ci`, `npx quasar prepare`, then `format:check`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `test` and `build`. Use `actions/setup-node` with `node-version-file` and npm caching. Reference: co2-calculator `quality-check.yml` and `test.yml`.\n4. **A security workflow** (`security.yml`), on PRs, pushes to `main`, weekly and on manual dispatch:\n   - `npm audit --audit-level=high` in `frontend/`\n   - CodeQL for `javascript-typescript`\n   - TruffleHog secret scan\n\n   Reference: co2-calculator `security.yml`.\n5. **Dependabot** (`.github/dependabot.yml`):\n   - `npm` for `/frontend` and `github-actions` for `/`\n   - target `dev`, label `dependencies`\n   - cooldowns of 7 days default, 30 major, 7 minor, 3 patch, with majors ignored, like co2-calculator\n   - add the `docker` ecosystem only if the image is kept (#38)\n6. **Image scanning, only if the Docker path is kept (#38).** The shared EPFL-ENAC `deploy.yml` already runs a Trivy scan on each image it builds; bump it from `v3.1.0` to the current `v3.10.0`. Add the weekly `registry-scan.yml` from `EPFL-ENAC/epfl-enac-build-push-deploy-action` (see its `docs/registry-scan.md`) to catch new CVEs in deployed images. If #38 removes the Docker path, skip this item.\n7. **Branch protection** on `dev` and `main`: require the quality job, and make the Pages deploy run only after it passes.\n\n**Acceptance criteria**\n- [ ] An unformatted file, a lint error, a type error and a failing test each turn the PR check red.\n- [ ] `format:check` reports `src/env.d.ts` (then it gets fixed).\n- [ ] Dependabot opens PRs against `dev`; `npm audit` and CodeQL run weekly.\n- [ ] `main` and `dev` reject merges when the quality job fails.\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\nKeep lefthook as the only definition and add `--check` variants there. That keeps CI coupled to a git-hook tool and keeps two meanings of \"format\".\n\n**Additional context**\nRaised in an architecture review of `dev` at `b35fc8c`. Related: #38 (deploy target).","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1791272564,"nonce":"j6ph6ZD6G4Me33LOoEYvpZctfok=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"RTE_lADOULtcMc8AAAABVIs2AM8AAAAHlcnLmA","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[TASK](CI) Make automated checks block broken code"},"title":"[TASK](